        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 1366706528,
        "heading": "Uses",
        "text": "The Shompen people of Great Nicobar Island, use the stems and branches in house construction, specifically as posts, roof beams, thatching rods and as wall-sticks.\nAdi people living in the Arunachal Pradesh, India, harvest the tender shoots of the plant to eat as a vegetable.\nThe plant is recorded as being used as a stimulant.",
